Theory: NdFeB Magnets
Strongest permanent magnets available.
Properties: - Remanence (Br): ≈1.0–1.5 T at 20°C - Coercivity (Hcb, Hcj): Depends on grade - Temperature effects: Br and Hcj decline
Grades: - N-series (80°C): Room temperature - M-series (100°C): Moderate temperature - H/SH/UH/EH (120–200°C): High temperature


